  "question": {
    "text": "The enthalpy changes for the following processes are listed below:\n$\\begin{array}{ll}\\mathrm{Cl}_2(\\mathrm{~g})=2 \\mathrm{Cl}(\\mathrm{g}), & 242.3 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1} \\\\ \\mathrm{I}_2(\\mathrm{~g})=2 \\mathrm{I}(\\mathrm{g}), & 151.0 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1} \\\\ \\mathrm{ICl}(\\mathrm{g})=\\mathrm{I}(\\mathrm{g})+\\mathrm{Cl}(\\mathrm{g}), & 211.3 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1} \\\\ \\mathrm{I}_2(\\mathrm{~s})=\\mathrm{I}_2(\\mathrm{~g}), & 62.76 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\end{array}$\nGiven that the standard states for iodine and chlorine are $\\mathrm{I}_2(\\mathrm{~s})$ and $\\mathrm{Cl}_2(\\mathrm{~g})$, the standard enthalpy of formation for $\\mathrm{ICl}(\\mathrm{g})$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "s9uhR",
      "text": "\n$-14.6 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ufCIr",
      "text": "\n$-16.8 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "acrRk",
      "text": "\n$+16.8 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "roeef",
      "text": "\n$+244.8 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{I}_2(\\mathrm{~s})+\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{Cl}_2 \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{ICl}(\\mathrm{g}) \\\\\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{H}=\\left[\\frac{1}{2} \\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{\\mathrm{b}_2(s) \\rightarrow k_2(g)}+\\frac{1}{2} \\mu_{1-1}+\\frac{1}{2} \\mu_{\\mathrm{cl}-\\mathrm{cl}}\\right]-\\left[\\mu_{1-a}\\right] \\\\\n& =\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 62.76+\\frac{1}{2} \\times 151.0+\\frac{1}{2} \\times 242.3\\right)-(211.3) \\\\\n& =228.03-211.3 \\\\\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{H}=16.73 \\\\\n&\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
